---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    NC Data Center Ledger collects public records on data-center decisions in North Carolina's
    Triad: meetings, agenda items and the documents behind them. Every item links to its official
    source, and every saved document carries the SHA-256 hash of the copy we retrieved. The project
    is free and open-source software.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/methodology/">Methodology and corrections</a>: how items get in, what the labels mean,
    who publishes this, how to cite it, and the corrections log.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fetcher">Our fetcher</h2>
  <p>
    If your site logged requests from a user agent starting with <code>dc-ledger/</code> and linking
    to this page, they came from this project. The fetcher:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>reads only public meeting and agenda information;</li>
    <li>
      follows <code>robots.txt</code> for the product token <code>dc-ledger</code>, and stays away
      from a site whose
      <code>robots.txt</code> it can't read;
    </li>
    <li>
      sends at most one request to a site every half second, and waits when a site asks it to;
    </li>
    <li>never gets around sign-ins, CAPTCHAs or bot walls.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To stop it, add this to your <code>robots.txt</code>, or ask through the{' '}
    <a href="/report/">report form</a>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>User-agent: dc-ledger
Disallow: /</code></pre>

  <h2 id="data">Using the data</h2>
  <p>
    Record IDs, page addresses, calendar UIDs, file paths and columns stay stable. A breaking change
    is announced at least 90 days ahead.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/data/#stability">Stability promise</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/data/#data-dictionary">Data dictionary</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions, a request to stop fetching, or to report a mistake, use the{' '}
    <a href="/report/">report form</a>. How corrections are handled is described under{' '}
    <a href="/methodology/#corrections">Corrections</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
